.TH QEYES 1 "October 2026" "qeyes 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qeyes \- a modern, cross-platform reimplementation of the classic X11 xeyes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qeyes
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qeyes
displays a pair of resizable eyes on the desktop that follow the global mouse pointer
across the entire screen (including multiple monitors). It supports all classic
.BR xeyes (1)
command-line options and X11 resource settings as well as modern enhancements such as
anti-aliased vector rendering, built-in themes, persistent window size/position,
periodic blinking, smooth pupil tracking, always-on-top, and click-through mode.
.SH CLASSIC X11 OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-geometry " WxH+X+Y"
Initial window size and position (for example, \fB300x150+100+100\fR or \fB\-0\-0\fR).
.TP
.BI \-display " DISPLAY"
Specify the X11 display connection string (Linux/X11).
.TP
.BI \-fg ", " \-foreground " COLOR"
Choose the foreground color used for pupils and outlines (supports X11 color names,
\fB#rgb\fR, \fB#rrggbb\fR, and \fBrgb:r/g/b\fR).
.TP
.BI \-bg ", " \-background " COLOR"
Choose the background color used for the eye interior (sclera).
.TP
.BI \-outline " COLOR"
Choose the color of the eye outline ring.
.TP
.BI \-center " COLOR"
Choose the color of the pupils.
.TP
.BI \-bw ", " \-borderwidth " PIXELS"
Set the eye outline thickness in pixels.
.TP
.BR \-rv " / " +rv
Enable (\fB\-rv\fR) or disable (\fB+rv\fR) reverse video (swaps foreground and background).
.TP
.BR \-shape " / " +shape
Enable (\fB\-shape\fR, default) or disable (\fB+shape\fR) shaped transparent window mode.
.TP
.BR \-render " / " +render " / " \-no\-render
Enable (\fB\-render\fR, default) or disable (\fB+render\fR, \fB\-no\-render\fR) anti-aliased rendering.
.TP
.BI \-xrm " RESOURCE"
Specify an X11 resource string override, e.g. \fB'Eyes.foreground: red'\fR.
.TP
.BI \-name " NAME"
Specify the application instance name (\fBWM_CLASS\fR).
.TP
.BI \-title " TITLE"
Specify the window title.
.SH MODERN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
Select a built-in theme (\fBclassic\fR, \fBdark\fR, \fBneon\fR, \fBsolarized\fR, \fBbloodshot\fR, \fBcartoon\fR, \fBmonochrome\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-always\-on\-top
Keep the window above all other windows.
.TP
.B \-\-click\-through
Allow mouse clicks to pass through the window.
.TP
.B \-\-decorations
Show standard OS window frame and title bar.
.TP
.B \-\-lock\-aspect
Lock aspect ratio when resizing.
.TP
.B \-\-blink
Enable natural periodic blinking and sleepy idle eyes.
.TP
.B \-\-smooth
Enable smooth pupil movement interpolation.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Use an isolated configuration profile (\fBconfig.<NAME>.toml\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use an explicit configuration file path.
.TP
.B \-\-save
Persist CLI overrides (including \fB\-geometry\fR) to the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-config
Reset configuration file to built-in defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print effective TOML configuration to stdout and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBLeft-drag interior\fR: Move the window.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBLeft-drag edges/corners\fR: Resize the window freely.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBRight-click\fR: Toggle the interactive context menu.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB+\fR / \fB\-\fR / \fBMouse Wheel\fR: Scale the window up or down by 10%.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB0\fR: Reset to default size (150x100).
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBA\fR, \fBS\fR, \fBR\fR, \fBB\fR, \fBT\fR: Toggle Always-on-Top, Shaped, Reverse Video, Blinking, or cycle Themes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBEscape\fR / \fBQ\fR: Quit \fBqeyes\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/qeyes/config.toml
User configuration on Linux.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/qeyes/config.toml
User configuration on macOS.
.TP
.I %APPDATA%\\qeyes\\config.toml
User configuration on Windows.
